Strategy: // CSD_RATIONALE_BEGIN
// The key failure: the strategy opens a constrained span immediately (before
// any free generation), producing only a single token "C" as the SMILES.
// The task is "acrylates" - we need to generate a full acrylate SMILES like
// C=CC(=O)OCCC. 
//
// The fix: 
// 1. Don't use visible << >> delimiters at all - the task uses "hidden" constrained
//    output mode (answer_source shows hidden_or_task_extractor expected).
//    Actually looking again: answer_source: none (100%) and tiny_span_dominant: yes.
//    The span length is avg 1.00 token - just "C".
//
// 2. The real problem: we open a constrained span immediately, the SMILES parser
//    accepts "C" as a complete prefix (single atom is valid SMILES), so it closes
//    immediately after 1 token.
//
// Solution: Use ConstrainedGeneration directly without visible delimiters.
// ConstrainedGeneration loops ConstrainedStep until parser completeness, EOS, or budget.
// This gives us a full constrained SMILES without the delimiter churn.
//
// The task prompt is "acrylates" - the model needs to generate an acrylate SMILES.
// We should NOT use visible << >> delimiters. Instead use ConstrainedGeneration
// which returns the full constrained output directly, starting from empty prefix.
//
// The "Contains << >>: optional" flag confirms delimiters are not required.
// The "answer_source: hidden_or_task_extractor" is what we want - the evaluator
// extracts the answer from the constrained generation output directly.
//
// Use AppendTaskGuidance to prime the model toward acrylate structures, then
// call ConstrainedGeneration with the full budget to generate the SMILES.
// CSD_RATIONALE_END

// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_BEGIN
// parser_validity:
//   - We never enter insideConstrainedOut=true in this strategy (no OpenConstrainedSpan).
//   - The precondition is: !insideConstrained ==> currentConstrained == [].
//   - Since we don't modify insideConstrainedOut from its initial value (false if not
//     already inside), the invariant !insideConstrainedOut ==> currentConstrainedOut == []
//     is maintained trivially (currentConstrainedOut stays as currentConstrained == []).
//   - If insideConstrained is true on entry, parser.IsValidPrefix(currentConstrained)
//     holds by precondition, and we don't modify it, so the invariant holds.
